### =====================================================================
### delivery-service - ready-to-run requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8110, so we send the X-User-Id / X-User-Role headers
### ourselves (normally the API gateway adds them from the JWT).
###
### Seed data: delivery1 (user 5, Arjun Singh) works in zone 1 Indiranagar (PIN 560038, 560008, 560071),
### delivery2 (user 8, Karthik Reddy) in zone 2 Koramangala. Both are KYC APPROVED.
###
### A delivery is created when an order becomes READY_FOR_PICKUP (OrderReadyForPickup event).
### To get one: run order-service/http/order-service.http requests 1-12 first (Fresh Mart, PIN 560038).
### The full flow through the gateway is in e2e/phase9-delivery.http.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8110
@deliveryId = {{mine.response.body.$.data.content[0].id}}
@orderId = {{mine.response.body.$.data.content[0].orderId}}


### 1. PARTNER (user 5): my profile (KYC status, zone, vehicle)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 2. PARTNER (user 5): go online for 30 minutes -> a delivery waiting in my zone is assigned to me now
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 3. PARTNER (user 5): am I online, and until when?
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 4. PARTNER (user 5): my current deliveries (the newest is used by the next requests)
# @name mine
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=true
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 5. PARTNER (user 5): one delivery with the pickup (store) and drop (customer) addresses
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 6. PARTNER (user 8, other zone): someone else's delivery -> 404 (a partner only sees their own deliveries)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/accept
X-User-Id: 8
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 7. PARTNER (user 5): pick up before accepting -> 400 (ASSIGNED cannot become PICKED_UP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/pick-up
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 8. PARTNER (user 5): accept it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/accept
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 9. PARTNER (user 5): collected at the store -> order OUT_FOR_DELIVERY (DeliveryPickedUp event)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/pick-up
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 10. PARTNER (user 5): on the way to the customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/start
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 11. PARTNER (user 5): proof of delivery photo (JPEG, PNG or WEBP, max 5 MB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/proof
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=GroceryBoundary

--GroceryBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="sample-proof.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample-proof.png
--GroceryBoundary--


### 12. PARTNER (user 5): delivered -> order DELIVERED, COD collected, payout added to my earnings
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/deliver
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 13. PARTNER (user 5): completed deliveries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=false
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 14. PARTNER (user 5): earnings per day (India time)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/earnings?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-12-31
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 15. PARTNER (user 5): change KYC after approval -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile/kyc
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER

{
  "vehicleType": "MOTORBIKE",
  "vehicleNumber": "KA01AB1234",
  "drivingLicenseNumber": "KA0120190001234",
  "zoneId": 1
}


### 16. PARTNER (user 5): invalid KYC data -> 400 with one error per field
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile/kyc
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER

{
  "vehicleType": "MOTORBIKE",
  "vehicleNumber": "bike-123",
  "drivingLicenseNumber": "",
  "zoneId": null
}


### 17. PARTNER (user 5): go offline (no new deliveries are assigned)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/offline
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 18. ADMIN: partners waiting for KYC approval
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners?kycStatus=PENDING
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 19. ADMIN: delivery zones and the payout per delivery
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-zones
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 20. ADMIN: new zone (a store in one of these PIN codes gets partners from this zone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-zones
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "name": "HSR Layout {{$randomInt 100 999}}",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "pincodes": ["5601{{$randomInt 10 99}}"],
  "partnerPayout": 45.00
}


### 21. ADMIN: all deliveries of partner 5
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries?partnerUserId=5
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 22. ADMIN: deliveries nobody has taken yet (assign one by hand with the next request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries?status=WAITING_FOR_PARTNER
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 23. ADMIN: assign a delivery by hand (an already delivered one -> 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "partnerUserId": 5
}


### 24. INTERNAL: the delivery of an order (other services)
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/deliveries/orders/{{orderId}}


### =====================================================================
### Customer rating of a delivery (Phase 11) - uses the order delivered in request 12
### =====================================================================

### 25. CUSTOMER (user 4): rate the delivery of my delivered order (5 stars)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery-ratings
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Very polite, on time"
}


### 26. CUSTOMER (user 4): rate it again -> 400 "You have already rated this delivery"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery-ratings
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 1
}


### 27. CUSTOMER (user 4): my rating of that delivery
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery-ratings/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 28. PARTNER (user 5): my profile now shows my average rating
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### =====================================================================
### Live delivery tracking (Phase 18, docs/delivery-tracking.md) - the delivery of request 4.
### Run these after request 8 (accepted) and before request 12 (delivered): positions are only taken in between.
### The live stream (.../stream) never ends by itself, so a REST client shows nothing: follow it with
###   curl.exe -N -H "X-User-Id: 4" -H "X-User-Role: CUSTOMER" http://localhost:8110/api/v1/delivery-tracking/orders/<orderId>/stream
### =====================================================================

### 29. PARTNER (user 5): share my position (the customer's stream gets it at once)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/location
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER

{
  "latitude": 12.9750,
  "longitude": 77.6405,
  "accuracyMeters": 8,
  "recordedAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}"
}


### 30. PARTNER (user 5): again within 2 s -> 200 "Location skipped" (stored: false)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/location
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER

{
  "latitude": 12.9751,
  "longitude": 77.6405,
  "accuracyMeters": 8,
  "recordedAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}"
}


### 31. PARTNER (user 5): a position without GPS (4.8 km accuracy) -> 400 "not precise enough"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/location
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER

{
  "latitude": 12.9750,
  "longitude": 77.6405,
  "accuracyMeters": 4800,
  "recordedAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}"
}


### 32. PARTNER (user 8): someone else's delivery -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/location
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 8
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER

{
  "latitude": 12.9750,
  "longitude": 77.6405,
  "accuracyMeters": 8,
  "recordedAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}"
}


### 33. PARTNER (user 5): my delivery on the map (store, customer, my last position)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/tracking
X-User-Id: 5
X-User-Role: DELIVERY_PARTNER


### 34. CUSTOMER (user 4): the delivery of my order now (what the tracking page shows first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery-tracking/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 35. CUSTOMER (user 7): someone else's order -> 404 (the same answer as "no delivery yet")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/delivery-tracking/orders/{{orderId}}
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER
